  "notes": "Timeline = gapless mp3 decode (same as data/audio.json); Demucs ran on that decode, so the stems need no shift. Method: (1) CTC emissions (20 ms frames) of the Demucs vocal stem from torchaudio MMS_FA (multilingual) and wav2vec2-large-lv60k-960h, each on the mono sum and on the left and right channels, fused as a probability mixture; (2) one global constrained Viterbi forced alignment of every line with a garbage 'star' token between lines; the Italian lyric is aligned with accents stripped and a few phonetic spellings (pron.py: F24, password, phishing); (3) signal refinement per unit on the vocal stem (rest onset, spectral flux onset, fricative start; ends at the next word when legato, else where the voice drops 15 dB); (4) cross-check against mlx-whisper large-v3-turbo (language it) word timestamps and the individual models/channels. Where Suno sang something other than the written lyric the source follows the singing: one 'Follia!' instead of two after 'qualcuno?', and the ad-lib 'futuro autocratico' twice after the break. conf: 0.35 + agreement of the independent alignments (<=60 ms) + CTC posterior + Whisper agreement. 'syl' = start/end of each spelled part."
